  "limitations": [
    "Only the final validated dataset is included. Earlier experimental results are excluded.",
    "Three independent trials per variant are not 15 independent trials; within-process repetitions are correlated.",
    "CDP instrumentation is disabled for wall/CPU trials; its omitted counts must not be interpreted as zero browser traffic. The process sampler remains enabled.",
    "CPU includes fixture-server and sampler overhead, uses short-duration OS counters, and can miss exited processes between samples.",
    "USS describes private pages, not total physical RAM; RSS sums duplicate shared pages, and unavailable Windows PSS stays null. Samples can miss peaks and uninspectable processes.",
    "Whole-trial USS includes setup, warmup, and cleanup. It does not establish steady-state active-work RAM savings.",
    "Idle zero refers to the dedicated worker and its tracked descendants, not the service or host.",
    "Worker reaping increases next-open latency; production grace/sweep defaults are 30/15 seconds rather than the benchmark's 2/1 seconds.",
    "Phase results are mixed: semantic CPU median increased from 209.375 to 268.75 milliseconds per operation; no semantic speed improvement is claimed.",
    "URL timeout latency includes the configured wait and final observation; CPU and command reductions do not imply an earlier specified timeout.",
    "CDP snapshot byte counts are compact UTF-8 JSON payload estimates, not exact WebSocket wire bytes. One separate metered trial per variant does not estimate population variance.",
    "Adapter work excludes MCP authentication, transport, production network isolation, and full service overhead. Windows results do not establish Raspberry Pi savings.",
    "Observation cleanup checks remaining attached children and temporary-profile removal; idle cleanup additionally checks retained process handles. Neither is a host-wide process audit.",
    "Benchmark success is distinct from regression-suite and CI status; no full-suite or CI completion is asserted here."
  ]
}
